<title>MOROCCO: Morocco reinforces sea links with West Africa.</title>
<headline>Morocco reinforces sea links with West Africa.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco has decided to strengthen its sea links with West Africa to try to promote Moroccan exports to the region, the fisheries ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A first link will cover the West Africa coast from Mauritania to South Africa, the ministry said. Another link will join the port of Casablanca to Angola and Cape Verde.</p>
<p>The state-owned Compagnie de Navigation Maritime (COMANAV) will also reinforce its presence in Ivory Coast, Ghana, Benin, Togo and Senegal, the ministry added.</p>
<p>Morocco's trade with West Africa remains insignificant as most exports go to Western Europe and North America.</p>
</text>
